## SQ-FLR-06 | processing inventories keep their items and Size 32 after a restart
@group A
@commands Place a crushing wheel and a saw holding items, save, restart on the same world
@pass items still there; `/data get block <controller>` shows `Size: 32`
@fails `ProcessingInventoryMixin.growOnLoad`
@from batches/r1111/a2.qb passed
# r1118 R4 A2 (2026-11-18): placing and filling rebuilt here (boot 1 of r1111 a1 was not migrated), then the restart in the
# row; the NBT gives Size 16, so a 32 read back is the mixin's grow on load kept through a save
> forceload add 2300 0 2310 10
sleep 2
> setblock 2300 -60 2 create:crushing_wheel_controller{Inventory:{Size:16,Items:[{Slot:0,id:"biomesoplenty:flesh",Count:16b}]}}
> setblock 2304 -60 2 create:mechanical_saw[facing=up]{Inventory:{Size:16,Items:[{Slot:0,id:"biomesoplenty:flesh",Count:16b}]}}
sleep 2
> save-all flush
sleep 5
restart
> forceload add 2300 0 2310 10
sleep 2
> data get block 2300 -60 2 Inventory
> data get block 2304 -60 2 Inventory
count Size: 32, Items: \[\{Slot: 0, id: "biomesoplenty:flesh", Count: 16b\}\] == 2

